Build note: The pre-converted MP4 is committed to the spike source tree alongside
  the prebuilt model binaries (models-prebuilt/). This avoids Wikimedia
  rate-limiting during snap builds while maintaining full license traceability.
  The go2rtc stream re-encodes the clip to h264 RTSP for consumer uniformity.

Content description:
  Munich pedestrian zone (Neuhauser Strasse), February 19, 2013. Low static
  camera position in a busy shopping street. Multiple pedestrians walk through
  the frame, some passing very close to the camera (filling ~50-70% of frame
  height). People are clearly visible and large — suitable for SSDLite/MobileNet
  person detection.  No vehicles in frame.

Frame-extraction evidence:
  Frames extracted with ffmpeg -vf fps=1 to scratchpad; frames 3 and 4 verified
  visually — multiple pedestrians occupy significant portion of the 1920×1080
  frame, upper bodies clearly visible, well-lit daytime scene.

